WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.540
STEPHANIE WONG:
What's up, everyone?

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:02.915
Thanks for checking
out This Week

00:00:02.915 --> 00:00:05.787
in Cloud, where we serve
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:07.620
Now, there's a lot of
great content at Next,

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.168
and I mean a lot,
so much that, well,

00:00:10.168 --> 00:00:12.210
sorting through all the
sessions to find the best

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.962
ones for you can be stressful.

00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:16.379
That's why every day this week,
we're publishing different

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:19.620
playlists of can't-miss
sessions based on subject area.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.200
Today's list-- data
management, AppDev,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.640
and cloud infrastructure.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.550
Check back later this week
for data analytics, security,

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.110
and machine learning.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.240
This week on the
GCP blog, learn how

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.782
to get the most out of Next.

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.240
Start building your
playlist today,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.420
because we're headed to Google
Next '19 in just under a month.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.670
And speaking of Next, if you
haven't earned your cloud

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.100
certifications yet, this could
be the perfect opportunity.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.285
Why get certified?

00:00:43.285 --> 00:00:44.910
Perhaps the fact that
our certification

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.890
for professional cloud
architect was just

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.410
named the top paying
IT certification.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.140
Or maybe you just want to show
the world what you can do.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.360
Any way you take it across
the industry, demand

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.460
for these roles is exploding,
and so has our list

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.350
of available certifications.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.930
We'll be offering these exams
at tons of convenient times

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.690
throughout Next, so go sign up.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.932
One of the big topics at
Next is machine learning.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.890
No matter what level of
machine learning you're

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.040
looking to get involved with,
Google has what you need.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.440
If you want to try training
a model without any code,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.000
you can use AutoML.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.820
But if you need a more complex
model and want to go deeper,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.740
you probably want
to use TensorFlow,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.330
which is easier to experiment
with, now more than ever,

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.110
thanks to our deep
learning VM instances.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.300
These instances are
spun up with TensorFlow

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.400
and other tools
pre-installed to get you up

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.750
and running right away.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.370
You can even include GPUs
while setting them up,

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.297
so see what you can build.

00:01:35.297 --> 00:01:37.380
Now, if you've ever been
extra concerned about who

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.172
might be reading your
email, have you heard

00:01:39.172 --> 00:01:41.010
about Gmail confidential mode?

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.810
Confidential mode
automatically removes

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.240
the option of forward, copy,
download, or print messages.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.810
It also lets you
set requirements,

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.640
so recipients must complete
a text message verification

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.610
prior to opening and viewing
an email that you send them.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.400
So that way, you can be sure
only your intended audience

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.870
can see what you've sent.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.790
Try out the beta by
clicking Confidential

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.027
Mode in Gmail's user settings.

00:02:02.027 --> 00:02:04.110
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.390
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.710
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.280
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.689
We'll see you in the cloud.

